From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes <hermes@lassul.us>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Unpack the bootstrap zip from the APK assets

droid-nix installs a Nix bootstrap instead of Termux's apt bootstrap. The
droid-nix build puts it into the APK as the asset bootstrap-aarch64.zip,
and the first start streams it from there: no dialog and no network.

Termux embeds its bootstrap in a native library (.incbin) and copies it
into a byte array; an asset needs no native code and is read as a
stream. This removes the termux-bootstrap native library (ndkBuild) and
the gradle tasks that downloaded Termux's bootstrap zips at build time.

The build.gradle part is based on nix-on-droid-app commit fe6512ed
("build.gradle: Remove unused bootstrap download tasks") by Zhaofeng Li.
